# (AI-assisted) Jak II: Dark Jak combo attacks in the slums. The "protect Kor and Kid" crash
# (reports/hw-oct25): the running-attack combo (target-darkjak.gc anon-function-10) calls
# combo-tracker-method-13, whose stack array was 16 bytes short for the array header that
# (method-of-type array new) zeroes; on the 3DS that wiped the caller's saved r4-r6.
# Native PC or C mode, e.g.
#   OPENGOAL_NO_SOUND=1 OPENGOAL_PAD_SCRIPT=jak2_darkjak.pad \
#     gk -g jak2 --proj-path <project> -- -boot -fakeiso -nosound -cbackend
# Expected: "darkjak: done" with Jak alive after the combos, then exit.
1000 continue ctysluma-start
1001 -
1002 wait *target* target-stance
1003 log darkjak: ctysluma-start
1004 pos *target*
1100 call pad-script-darkjak
1101 -
